Read `ENGINEERING.md` before implementation. These shared rules apply to Codex and Claude Code; follow applicable nested instructions too. The factory is a separate harness, not this app's origin or an automatic instruction ancestor.

- Implement the requested frontend and real server/API backend. A static page or mocked browser response does not satisfy a full-stack request. Choose a suitable stack; do not add persistence or a cloud service without a product need.
- Define the server contract, validate input, return safe errors, keep secrets server-only and implement authentication/authorization where required. Verify browser → API → data/response behavior.
- Fill the app-owned commands and operational contract in `ENGINEERING.md`; pin dependencies, commit lockfiles and implement independent CI/CD. Run meaningful tests, typecheck/build and browser checks before reporting success.
- Work only in this repository. Preserve user files and dirty work, verify fetch/push origin before external writes, and use the approved branch workflow. Do not force-push, change visibility or delete to recover.
- Reuse the human-approved bounded run scope for routine steps. Check provider identity/target immediately before actions. Scope, credentials/IAM, core exposure, production/protection or budget changes and required action-time approvals remain gates. These instructions do not grant provider authority.
- Apply source/run/project provenance and exact private resource inventory. Keep credentials, state and private provider configuration out of source and logs; do not load arbitrary `.env` as shell code or copy factory execution credentials into app CI.
- Reconcile unknown mutation outcomes without duplicate creates/deploys. Keep source durable through authorized Git push or private export/restore before ending; a workspace-local bundle/hash is not recovery acceptance.

This seed contains operating rules, not a completed app, configured deployment, approved resource plan or live verification. Keep it current as the app evolves and record actual evidence separately.
